course: dictionary
lesson: 9924
title: Tangy: taste and smell words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something tastes or smells. Tangy is one of them. It means sharp, strong and pleasant, often a little sour, like lemon, lime or orange.
explain: Check the context: «Bacteria in yoghurt turn milk sugar into lactic acid, which makes it thick and tangy.» Yoghurt is not just sweet milk, so the sharp, sour taste is the tangy part.
explain: Tangy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «the tangy smell of the sea». It can change form too: tangier and tangiest compare how strong the taste is. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Tangy means sharp, strong and pleasant, often a little sour.
fact: Tangy can describe a taste or a smell, as in «the tangy smell of the sea».
fact: Yoghurt is milk changed by friendly bacteria, which make lactic acid, and that acid is what makes it tangy.
fact: «Live cultures» on a pot means the friendly bacteria are still in the yoghurt.
fact: Tangier and tangiest are comparison forms, like sweeter and sweetest.
exercise: «The tangy smell of the sea» tells you the smell is what? | Sweet like sugar | Loud like a drum | *Sharp and fresh | Soft and warm
exercise: What makes yoghurt tangy? | Sugar sprinkled on from a spoon | Cold air from the fridge | *Lactic acid made by friendly bacteria | Food colouring
exercise: Which word in «Friendly bacteria turn milk into tangy yoghurt» tells you about the taste? | milk | bacteria | yoghurt | *tangy
test: Which word is closest in meaning to tangy? | *Sharp | Cold | Soft | Quiet
test: Complete the sentence: The lime juice tasted so ___ that I pulled a face. | *tangy | Silent | Soggy | Fluffy
exam: Which sentence uses tangy correctly? | *The lemon drink was tangy and fresh. | The pillow was tangy and soft. | The sky was tangy at noon. | The clock was tangy and loud.
